    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, you're asking me because I was too short to fly. I had a dream to become a fighter pilot. I actually got that dream once I had to be Air Force Academy. And I found out that just because I was a girl, they wouldn't let me fly fighters. And it just pissed me off. So, but then I had another obstacle and it was a little bit too short. You got to be five four or a little bit shorter than that. My sitting height was okay. So in my quest in order to be able to fly, I hung upside down in the hallway in my dorm area at the Air Force Academy. It helped a little bit, and you get measured in the morning, by the way, but it wasn't quite enough. I still had to get an exception to policy after a couple of years of struggle with the bureaucracy. I fit in the cockpit, I could function, but the bureaucrats kept saying no, but we eventually prevailed.",
