    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74167.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "Well, I wasn't focused on that, but, you know, being in that pioneering group, and there were many pioneers before me, like the Women World War II pilots who were just amazing role models for me. I mean, we were on that cutting edge, breaking down that barrier, so I was very aware that we were breaking through those barriers because when they opened the door, they selected seven of us to go. But at the time, I was just trying to show that the airplane doesn't care if you're a boy or a girl. They just care if you fly well and you're too straight and being a part of the squadron and building my skills.",
