    "turn_text": "Hmm. Well, Michael, this is a very long story. It's hard to answer in just 30 seconds. But as someone, look, I lost my dad when I was 12. And then I was preyed upon and trusting my track coach who was over twice my age in a position of authority, took away my innocence. And later on in the military, I experienced such a harassment and sexual assault. And so for me and my journey, and everyone has their own journey and look There's so many women and men out there who have been through sexual abuse and sexual assault and we each deal with it differently And I just want to encourage anyone who's listening if you've been through this 50 years ago or you went through it last night There's hope for you and the one reason I shared my journey is to provide a light out of the darkness that you can thrive through the darkness and in my own journey I've had a days in the fetal position and despair. And this was a really dark experience as I went through. But what I found was I had to come to a place of peace and I had to come to a place of forgiveness. I used the quote, bitterness is the pill you swallow, hope any other person dies. And I'll tell you, your perpetrator, those who are listening, you're a silent, your abuser, they already robbed you of enough. Don't let them rob you of your future. Don't let them rob you of the gift of today. You've got to find your own path to peace. And for me, it didn't happen easily and it didn't happen until many years later. I had to, in my heart and in my spirit and by the grace of God, come to a place of forgiveness that's not the same as reconciliation, that's not the same as going back and somehow befriending your abuser. It's just releasing the anger and the venom in your soul and your heart over what you went through and giving that over to God and providing that forgiveness, you know, just like we are forgiven in our own lives, certainly not for things that grave. But it's the same principle that brought freedom for me to be able to heal and have that peace. And I'd encourage anyone to take that path, your own path, your own individual path who's listening right now.",
