    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74167.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Well, the MacGyver story in there to fly is, you know, they transitioned us into fighters, but nobody thought about we're going to be on these long missions. My longest mission was 11 and a half hours across the Atlantic Ocean. You're in the jet for like another hour or more on before and after. My longest combat mission was 9.3 hours. Nobody thought about how are the women going to pee. We're in a single-seat cockpit. You've got all your gear on. And everyone just looked at me and I'm like, what? This isn't kindergarten. Like, this is not talking about PPE. Like, we've got to figure this out. It's a safety issue. And so I tried, I'm no kidding, looked around my garage. I'm like, what else can I do to make this work? And so it's my MacGyver moment. And so I figured out that, And we could velcro the inseam of my flight suit and use a funnel that civilian pilots use is a little complicated. I had to try it out a lot. But my first time, I tried the whole system out in Iraq. The sergeant in charge of intel got up and said, our objectives today are to deter Saddam Hussein, you know, a couple of objectives. And then Captain McSally is going to take a piss over Iraq today.",
